-- title:
--   Geometric integrality of the Gauss branches of the X₁(Mp) two-chart model
-- statement:
--   Fix a prime $p$ and an integer $M \ge 5$ with $M \neq 0$ in the relevant sense and $p \nmid M$. Let $L$ be a field of characteristic zero that is a cyclotomic extension of $\mathbb{Q}$ for $\{p\}$, and let $\zeta \in L$ be a primitive $p$-th root of unity. Let $K$ be the intermediate field of $L \subseteq \mathrm{LaurentSeries}(L)$ obtained as `laurentBaseChange`, i.e. the subfield generated over $L$ by the image, under the coefficientwise map $\mathrm{LaurentSeries}(\mathbb{Q}) \to \mathrm{LaurentSeries}(L)$ induced by $\mathbb{Q} \to L$, of the $q$-expansion function field `x1FunctionFieldC` of $\Gamma_1(Mp)$ over $\mathbb{Q}$. Let $A$ be a discrete valuation domain with fraction field $L$, whose maximal ideal contains $p$ and is generated by $\varpi$, and such that $\zeta$ lies in the image of $A \to L$; assume $A$ acts on $K$ compatibly with $A \to L \to K$. Let $j \in K$ be nonzero with underlying Laurent series the image of `jq` $= q^{-1}\cdot(\text{power series } j_{\mathrm{num}}$ over $\mathbb{Q})$ under the coefficientwise map. Let $k$ be an algebraically closed field with an $A$-algebra structure sending $\varpi$ to $0$. Write $A_{\mathrm{fin}} =$ `chartAlgFin` $A\,K\,j$ for the $A$-subalgebra of elements of $K$ integral over $A[j]$. Then for every prime $\mathfrak{P}$ of $A_{\mathrm{fin}}$ that is minimal over the ideal generated by the image of $\varpi$, the ring $k \otimes_A (A_{\mathrm{fin}}/\mathfrak{P})$ is a domain.
--
--   This is the geometric integrality of the branches of the special fibre at $p$ of the two-chart integral model of $X_1(Mp)$ over $\mathbb{Z}_{(p)}[\zeta_p]$: each irreducible component of the fibre, given by a prime minimal over the uniformiser, remains irreducible and reduced after base change to any algebraically closed field of residue characteristic $p$, the classical Igusa–Deligne–Rapoport description of the two Gauss branches. It is used downstream in the analysis of the special fibre of the model, in particular in identifying its irreducible components with the two charts' branch ideals and in computing the branch ideals in the stalks.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_ModularCurve_XOneP_isDomain_tensorProduct_quotient_of_mem_minimalPrimes_span_of_map_eq_zero_twoChartModel_x1_mul.lean

